<title>UK: DIARY - Today in Westminster - Nov 1.</title>
<headline>DIARY - Today in Westminster - Nov 1.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Parliament will debate schools at its shortened Friday session starting at 0930 GMT.</p>
<p>Junior education minister Robin Squire leads off for the government, followed by Labour education and employment spokesman Peter Kilfoyle.</p>
<p>The adjournment debate at 1430 GMT is on policing the streets, opened by Liberal Democrat MP Chris Davies.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 44-171-542 7767</p>
</text>
